 ],
 "literal": "Like he who thinks, does he not think? I wonder; the sneeze, like budding, disappears.",
 "translation": "Does my lover seem to think of me, but then stop? For my sneeze, which was about to burst forth, has subsided and disappeared.",
 "modern": "அவர் என்னை நினைப்பவர் போலத் தொடங்கிப் பின் நினையாமல் விட்டுவிடுகிறாரோ? ஏனெனில், வரவிருந்த தும்மல் அரும்புவது போலத் தோன்றிப் பின் அடங்கிவிடுகிறது.",
 "explanation": "This couplet draws on the traditional Tamil belief that a sneeze is triggered when a loved one thinks of you. The heroine feels a sneeze beginning to form in her nose, which is described beautifully as 'சினைப்பது' (budding like a flower). However, the sneeze suddenly fades away ('கெடும்') without happening. She wonders if her distant lover started to think of her, but then immediately stopped, causing her physical sneeze to abort mid-way.",
